            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">JOIN 2 tables</span>
                </div>
                <p>Join <code>STUDENT</code> to <code>LOGIN_ACCOUNT</code> and show each student's full name, username, and last login date.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">JOIN 3 tables</span>
                </div>
                <p>Show every member of <code>Coding Collective</code> with their role and year group. Sort by role, then last name.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">JOIN 3 tables</span>
                </div>
                <p>List the club name, meeting day, student full name, and role for all memberships. Order first by meeting day, then club name.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">Filter joined data</span>
                </div>
                <p>Show only Year 12 students and the clubs they attend.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.3.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">Date filter</span>
                </div>
                <p>Return usernames and last-login dates for accounts that were used on or after <code>2026-03-09</code>.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="sql-sheet-section">
        <div class="sql-section-heading">
            <span class="sql-section-number">4</span>
            <div>
                <h2>Schema and ERD Thinking</h2>
                <p>Use the dataset to explain the database design, not just query it.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <ol class="sql-task-list">
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.2.1</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">Schema levels</span>
                </div>
                <p>Give one example of what belongs in the conceptual schema, logical schema, and physical schema for this clubs system.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sql-task">
                <div class="sql-task-top">
                    <span class="sql-task-tag">A3.2.2</span>
                    <span class="sql-task-focus">Modality</span>
                </div>
                <p>Explain the likely modality between <code>STUDENT</code> and <code>LOGIN_ACCOUNT</code>, then compare it with the modality between <code>STUDENT</code> and <code>MEMBERSHIP</code>.</p>
